[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137257,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is a benign congenital developmental lesion of lenticular anlage, composed of extraocular crystalline lens tissue and its basement membrane.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137258,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137259,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LA14.0Y Other specified structural developmental anomalies of eyelids</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137260,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> Zimmerman tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137261,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137262,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma generally occurs deep in the medial lower eyelid. Cases with exclusive involvement of the inferior anterior orbit, lacrimal sac, nasolacrimal duct, and extraocular muscles have been reported {30407999;10406159;5542122;34750316}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137263,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present in infancy with a smooth, firm, slowly growing subcutaneous mass in the medial lower eyelid, already present at birth. On imaging, the tumour is solid, well circumscribed, and contrast enhancing, without bone erosion {34750316;26070367}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137264,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is extremely rare, with &lt;&nbsp;30&nbsp;cases reported worldwide. There is a slight male predominance (68%) {34750316}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137265,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a developmental abnormality.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137266,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Two hypotheses have been proposed as to the origin of the lesion: formation of an additional lens vesicle locus from surface ectoderm {5542122}, and displacement or migration of cells from the lens placode {973823;16102745}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137267,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma macroscopically appears as an ovoid, white-grey, firm mass, measuring as large as 20&nbsp;mm {1390539;34750316}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137268,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma has a characteristic morphological appearance and consists of islands of cuboidal to polygonal cells, reminiscent of lens epithelium, and bladder (Wedl) cells surrounded by a thick layer of eosinophilic PAS-positive material analogous to lens capsule. Psammomatous calcification can be seen. Dense collagenous stroma is present in the background {5542122}.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is not required for diagnosis. The epithelial and bladder cells stain positively for vimentin, S100, PAX8, and lens crystalline proteins, and are negative for cytokeratins {34750316;36249298}. Electron microscopy demonstrates 10&nbsp;nm whorled cytoplasmic microfilaments within degenerating epithelial cells {973823}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137269,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137270,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137271,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> extraocular crystalline lens tissue and dense collagen bundles surrounded by a PAS-positive membrane localized to the eyelid/orbit.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137272,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137273,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 43,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Phakomatous choristoma is benign. Malignant transformation has not been described. Simple resection is curative {34750316}. Rare associations include myopia, colobomatous hypoplastic optic disc, and staphyloma {16424545}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]